  ],
  "notes": "out_public_subnets: a template whose public-subnet choice defaults to off has its public-list output excluded under defaults, so the second branch accepts a two-valued choice parameter defaulting to false/no instead (weaker, rare). The private route table needs no default route, so none is checked. 'carved out of the VPC's own IPv4 range' cannot be checked as containment; CidrBlock presence stands in. Real templates reviewed: OneShot_DSV4F puts AmazonProvidedIpv6CidrBlock on AWS::EC2::VPC (not a VPC property, no IPv6 range is associated) and GLM53F gives subnets no IPv6 range; both correctly fail."
